From 1352af3b01d4aae916be3af61da4758b3fabecd4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 23:22:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 360/361] hir_typeck: `type_is_clone` waits on an unresolved
 projection, as `type_is_copy` does

jaq-core 3.1.2 src/filter.rs:600 (jaq 3.1.2), `Id::paths`:
    Ast::Pipe(l, Some(pat), r) => flat_map_then_with(l.run(proj_cv(&cv)), cv, move |y, cv| {
        bind_run(pat, r, cv, y, |f, cv| f.paths(cv))
    })
= "Failed to find an impl of Clone for (<_659 as DataT>::V<'_>, List<<_659 as DataT>::V<'_>>)". The inner closure,
coerced to bind_run's `fn(Cv<'a, D, T>)` pointer, calls the generic `paths::<_659>`, whose parameter type spells the
projection `<_659 as DataT>::V`; the coercion sets bind_run's `T` to a tuple holding it (G5 trace: pass 2, coercion
checking), and bind_run's `T: Clone` is checked in that pass's associated-type stage, before the outer closure's
parameter (typed from `flat_map_then_with`'s `impl Fn(U, T)`) pins `_659` to `D`. The builtin tuple Clone rule
(find_trait_impls_magic -> type_is_clone) asked about the projection: `DataT::V`'s bound is `ValT`, which has `Clone`
only as a supertrait, so no bound and no impl matched and `type_is_clone` returned Unequal -> a hard "No impl".
`type_is_copy` already returned Fuzzy for an unbound path; `type_is_clone` now does the same.

Kit clone-projection-ivar-test: jaq.rs (the shape, 2021 + 2024; fails on 0359 and 0324), neg.rs (`(NotClone, u32)` is
still rejected). The stand-in core has no written tuple Clone impl, as 1.90's libcore: a written
`impl<A: Clone, B: Clone> Clone for (A, B)` hides the bug (the impl search accepts it fuzzily).

Assisted-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context)
---

diff --git a/src/hir_typeck/helpers.cpp b/src/hir_typeck/helpers.cpp
index d1b1a8b5..61c63b9a 100644
--- a/src/hir_typeck/helpers.cpp
+++ b/src/hir_typeck/helpers.cpp
@@ -4615,6 +4615,13 @@ bool TraitResolution::trait_contains_type(const Span& sp, const ::HIR::GenericPa
             return ::HIR::Compare::Fuzzy;
         }
         else {
+            // A projection not resolved yet (`<_ as DataT>::V`: its type is still an ivar) may well be `Clone`: wait, as
+            // `type_is_copy` does. jaq-core 3.1.2 filter.rs:600: a tuple `(<_659 as DataT>::V, List<..>)` (bind_run's `T`,
+            // from the signature of the generic `paths::<_659>` its closure argument calls) was checked against the
+            // builtin tuple `Clone` impl in the same pass that set it, before `_659` was known -> "No impl" -> error.
+            if( type.data().is_Path() && type.data().as_Path().binding.is_Unbound() ) {
+                return ::HIR::Compare::Fuzzy;
+            }
             return ::HIR::Compare::Unequal;
         }
         }
